<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:45Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>What makes 'Grand Theft Auto VI' more than just a game?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39496e37f5600f0cc33dd37065e56302ca01b4bef22b3f35545a110583e926e1</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-makes-grand-theft-auto-vi-more-than-just-a-game/a-79965822--24b2767125c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-makes-grand-theft-auto-vi-more-than-just-a-game/a-79965822?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When "GTA VI" is released on November 19, millions of people worldwide will rush to their consoles to play it. How has this video game created such a cross-generational buzz?</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64ea71601b741faa16f123988b9f2f832d61576b44a609a94a7962a7cfb90ad1</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms and the Nvidia scandal has cast doubt on Anthropic's IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Crimean Bridge has been attacked again, Russian official says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be4f349917eef799c013e6fb719e549e6bc6bf350eb30fb11a6aefb7721c30ba</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T03:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/crimean-bridge-has-been-attacked-again-russian-official-says/a-79986700--99815dc85f47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/crimean-bridge-has-been-attacked-again-russian-official-says/a-79986700?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Crimean Bridge has been attacked again, Crimea's Russian-installed governor said. The attack comes as Vladimir Putin prepares to sit down with Donald Trump and Xi Jinping for joint talks in China.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's allies gather in Berlin for 'Coalition of the Willing' summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8de1bf02664982654f203d7774cfd67d16fe95d18fe77b0f49092b4d06a4ccf9</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T02:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-allies-gather-in-berlin-for-coalition-of-the-willing-summit/live-79986520--4d9de08ae023.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-allies-gather-in-berlin-for-coalition-of-the-willing-summit/live-79986520?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's European backers are convening in Berlin, with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner also set to attend the meeting. Follow the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Almost 1 in 4 children live in conflict zones — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0eeaf4ad570c9f76a9193bee72d000fb13fd3d1fdd864a124917dfe1369ce324</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T00:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/almost-1-in-4-children-live-in-conflict-zones-report/a-79979203--07598193af0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/almost-1-in-4-children-live-in-conflict-zones-report/a-79979203?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Denial of humanitarian access, abductions and sexual violence are among several violations against children that have increased dramtically over the past year, according to a new report by Save the Children.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Grand Theft Auto VI launches to global fanfare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94fc2ec19ac88a1843e0c437257a9fc95bca8813e0e058f0ca90b07ba3670fd1</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T23:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/grand-theft-auto-vi-launches-to-global-fanfare/a-79986461--a4bcdbd4f395.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/grand-theft-auto-vi-launches-to-global-fanfare/a-79986461?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After 13 years of waiting, fans around the world will get to play the latest installment in the blockbuster video game series. In focus: A tale of crime and violence in a fictionalized version of Miami.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What the Crimean bridge attack means for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a1a042734d153495282d47cecdf55b88ab4d85d59e46461e8284302e0d65a03</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-crimean-bridge-attack-means-for-russia/a-79985991--1ee630640446.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-crimean-bridge-attack-means-for-russia/a-79985991?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's latest strike on the Kerch Bridge has disrupted a key transport link between Russia and Crimea. Beyond the damage, the attack could have serious consequences for Russian military logistics and Putin's prestige.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>US Pentagon chief Hegseth signs military deal in Venezuela</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89a81eb4ba997578e413dfafa05640100dd488bee0211edd6ae2c41ec397b2f0</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T20:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-pentagon-chief-hegseth-signs-military-deal-in-venezuela/a-79985607--34c2cd46bf99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-pentagon-chief-hegseth-signs-military-deal-in-venezuela/a-79985607?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On a visit to Caracas, Pete Hegseth signed a deal that signifies the "reestablishment of our defense partnership." US-Venezuela ties were strained for years until US troops ousted ex-President Nicolas Maduro in January.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Would Ukraine trade land for NATO membership or protection?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fa88b29a492cdd2f4cff59e23a6bc9b4311fc415de2c17c3f787046b7145918</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T18:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/would-ukraine-trade-land-for-nato-membership-or-protection/a-79984492--4bee4478ee59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/would-ukraine-trade-land-for-nato-membership-or-protection/a-79984492?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is exploring whether Ukraine would cede parts of Donetsk province still under its control in return for NATO membership or protection. Experts warn the idea is risky.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Israel launches new ground operation in Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0255b54f9c308199f818927d2fe3d11ac532d4848b7671857caf9e5ffcddb14</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T18:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-launches-new-ground-operation-in-gaza/a-79984958--35417a49cd93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-launches-new-ground-operation-in-gaza/a-79984958?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israel has said its military is targeting Hamas infrastructure in central Gaza and urged civilians to avoid the area. The fight is unfolding against the backdrop of a dire food and shelter situation for Palestinians.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Muslims to outnumber Christians by 2035, research shows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d591588f0356ee14a559febd2bc3740ba9a6e357c412ef0d540153e6453d89c3</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/muslims-to-outnumber-christians-by-2035-research-shows/a-79984307--31fefd620e5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/muslims-to-outnumber-christians-by-2035-research-shows/a-79984307?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pew Research Center projections show that there will be 2.57 billion Muslims and 2.52 billion Christians by 2035. Researchers say differences in fertility rates account for the change.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US House Democrats nominate Hakeem Jeffries for speaker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8fedc175b90d0668cf2eefeb506659a91b7cfb42e0f90b1ce38969f0ef2a9e5b</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-house-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-for-speaker/a-79983827--f53f68cb3405.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-house-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-for-speaker/a-79983827?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jeffries is set to be the first Black speaker of the US House of Representatives when Democrats take control of the chamber next year. He will be second in line to the presidency.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund bows to fan pressure and end Rheinmetall deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b793914863f9f2f948c8906f3919189b7d39ccc6f356fd16bbccad61cf84cc4</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121--2c9b64a964f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Borussia Dortmund has reluctantly ended its association with a major sponsor after long-term fan protests. They are not the first Bundesliga club to u-turn, as commercial interests clash with politics and fan culture.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea expanded uranium enrichment plant, says IAEA head</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fba2d00c63a241facdf3e759940af3befc5a3b5474697d68507e8b840db2d51d</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expanded-uranium-enrichment-plant-says-iaea-head/a-79982758--65619f1023d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expanded-uranium-enrichment-plant-says-iaea-head/a-79982758?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">IAEA chief Rafael Grossi has said the ongoing expansion of North Korea's uranium enrichment program remains "a cause for serious concern."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Coalition of the Willing' meets in Berlin: Europe remains committed to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2eded031720f93eb2bd4854520349b5e8c59f3c4beadfe49b01f725015057b8d</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/coalition-of-the-willing-meets-in-berlin-europe-remains-committed-to-ukraine/a-79974996--9529e6865e8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/coalition-of-the-willing-meets-in-berlin-europe-remains-committed-to-ukraine/a-79974996?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The "Coalition of the Willing" supporting Ukraine is gathering in Berlin. One of the key issues under discussion is whether Europe will be able to play a role in future negotiations over the country's future.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Has the 'Parthenon puzzle' been solved? The long quest to reassemble lost eastern pediment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca7766f8a8cfe65f19a5d18382be2c8ce103bc4d69709eee55822f5f707a20b2</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098--4f23b2ccbfc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The depiction of the birth of the goddess Athena above the Parthenon's entrance is considered a masterpiece of ancient art. Now, a German research team has pieced together all the surviving fragments.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India: Online censorship grows after 'Cockroach' protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b6791c116c73e1b19525339a96e584406764181cd538e24143b3f13117c367c</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-online-censorship-grows-after-cockroach-protests/a-79976982--a74d2015326f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-online-censorship-grows-after-cockroach-protests/a-79976982?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since anti-government Cockroach protests erupted, journalists and creators say their content is increasingly being restricted on social media in India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>ICJ to rule on Rohingya genocide case against Myanmar: What to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3dd01c946608cdaa64ed421138a7d8f84a9370bf45be51108d101626e753874</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/icj-to-rule-on-rohingya-genocide-case-against-myanmar-what-to-know/a-79981434--76de3c2375bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/icj-to-rule-on-rohingya-genocide-case-against-myanmar-what-to-know/a-79981434?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ICJ is set to decide whether Myanmar's military operations in Rakhine State a decade ago were carried out with the intent to destroy the country's Rohingya minority, in whole or in part.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Axes and cutlasses: Violence on Nigeria's election campaign trail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65db7b82279014f0ea6a1dce0722a5e94fea7529e9f1b9aa207b0f1d6b27675e</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T10:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/axes-and-cutlasses-violence-on-nigeria-s-election-campaign-trail/a-79978467--351fdc554734.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/axes-and-cutlasses-violence-on-nigeria-s-election-campaign-trail/a-79978467?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria's January 2027 elections approach, political violence and thuggery at campaign rallies and town hall meetings raise concerns about voter safety.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Latin America's mega-prisons: Can El Salvador's model work?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:419e4a95d81a88f229f58565e9ecfb99484413e825ceb61b4e855693e589475f</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:40:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T10:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/latin-america-s-mega-prisons-can-el-salvador-s-model-work/a-79973524--e4fa38fb46de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/latin-america-s-mega-prisons-can-el-salvador-s-model-work/a-79973524?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">El Salvador's mega-prison has become a model for governments across Latin America seeking to combat organized crime. But experts question whether the approach is effective, sustainable or compatible with human rights.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>APEC summit: Xi, Trump and Putin to hold first-ever trilateral in China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40b64cb8385e9d954352dbf274d80b53f21587be6cba7b1976769ce01cfe6ebb</id><updated>2026-11-19T07:41:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-xi-trump-and-putin-to-hold-first-ever-trilateral-in-china/live-79964719--b3026ef56b63.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-xi-trump-and-putin-to-hold-first-ever-trilateral-in-china/live-79964719?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The three world leaders are expected to discuss the wars in Ukraine and Iran, as well as nuclear arms controls. The talks come amid Trump's tour of Asia that began in the Philippines. Follow DW live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
